### Liveness check — no DB dependency
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

### Readiness check — confirms the app can see the migrated schema
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/db

### Register a user
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "you@example.com",
  "password": "choose-a-real-password",
  "timezone": "Asia/Singapore"
}

### Login (form-encoded — this is what OAuth2PasswordRequestForm expects)
# @name login
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=you@example.com&password=choose-a-real-password

### Create a flexible Commitment (uses the token from the login response above)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "flexible",
  "title": "Write essay",
  "category": "study",
  "estimated_duration_minutes": 300,
  "due_at": "2026-10-05T23:59:00+08:00"
}

### List your commitments
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/commitments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Current week's capacity snapshot — the actual point of the whole schema
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/capacity/current
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
